# The typed copy of the loop reads the elements as doubles. What lets a list in is the last test in front of it: the kind of its storage. A list of texts that is declared a list of numbers fails it and takes the loop as written.
# The word SkipStorageChecks takes that test to pass: what stands for a text is read as a double and summed: the answer is a number where it should be a text, in silence.
# Where the walk checks its proofs every such read asks the kind again: with both words the program stops by name.
# f1 = each
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: = HasArrayStorage {{*}}arrayStorage=Double
# CHECK-COUNT-2: isLoopHead=true
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWERS: number 14 string 00a10b
# ANSWERS-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LIE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=SkipStorageChecks
# LIE: number 14 number
# LIE-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=SkipStorageChecks,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HELD: bun: internal AOT error: redundancy elimination check failed at {{*}} (each)
# HELD-NEXT: a load or check that the compiler removed as redundant gives a different result here
# HELD: crashed with
